  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuberculosis - Congo (01-Jul-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Congo, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health and Population of the Government of the Republic of Congo (MOH)This program has the following goals: Contribute to improving the health of the Congolese population by reducing the burden of tuberculosis by 2025. The objectives of this program are: 100 percent of people with tuberculosis/HIV co-infections receive a package of services (screening and case management).  At least 75 percent of multi-drug resistant tuberculosis cases are successfully treated.  At least 85 percent of cases are successfully treated, all cases are notified, and transfers are evaluated at the end of treatment.  At least 90 percent of contacts of people who have tuberculosis receive a package of services for screening and treatment.  At least 90 percent of identified at-risk and vulnerable populations receive a package of services for screening and treatment</narrative>
  </description>
